 add(notes,'p','The base preference ranking retains descriptive outcome, effort and source context. An explicitly experimental exploration bonus is bounded at 25 selection points and decreases with supporting observations; compatible small-pattern clues can help a low-cost unfamiliar experiment be considered. Selection points are not happiness points or probabilities. No predictive guarantee has been established. When evidence is scant, WAM says so.');
